    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute \\(x\\) into the expression:**\n   When \\(x = 3\\), the expression becomes \\((2(3) + 5)^2\\).\n\n2. **Simplify the expression inside the parentheses:**\n   \\[\n   2(3) + 5 = 6 + 5\n   \\]\n\n3. **Perform the addition inside the parentheses:**\n   \\[\n   6 + 5 = 11\n   \\]\n\n4. **Square the result from the previous step:**\n   Since squaring a number simply multiplies the number by itself, we have:\n   \\[\n   11^2 = 11 \\times 11\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the square:**\n   \\[\n   11 \\times 11 = 121\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).",
